Give the Meson build path the same ANSI C prototype macros the Autoconf path
defines, so the header it renders actually compiles.

src/dbinc/db.in is a template: db.h is rendered from it by substituting @VAR@
placeholders. Its function-pointer struct members are written in the traditional
Berkeley DB style, and db.h deliberately does not include db_config.h, so the
__P() wrapper they use has to be defined by the template itself. db.in therefore
carries two dedicated slots for it, @DB_PROTO1@ and @DB_PROTO2@, whose values
dist/configure.ac computes at configure time:

    DB_PROTO1="#undef __P"
    DB_PROTO2="#define	__P(protos)	protos"     # ac_cv_prog_cc_c89 = yes

The Meson path renders the same template through dist/meson/gen_header.py, but
its substitution table left both slots as empty strings. gen_header.py replaces
a placeholder with whatever the table holds -- an empty string erases the macro
rather than leaving the placeholder behind -- so a Meson build emits a db.h that
uses __P((...)) more than 400 times while never defining __P:

    dist/db.h:529:14: error: expected ';' at end of declaration list
            int (*close) __P((DB_LOGC *, u_int32_t));

Every translation unit that includes db.h fails (db_int.h includes it), so the
Meson build -- the only build path this recipe uses -- cannot produce a library
at all. The Autoconf path is unaffected, and the Android build shipped in the
tree carries the same two lines (build_android/db.h), which is what the correct
output looks like.

The values below are the ones configure.ac selects for an ANSI C compiler, which
is what clang is here (-std=c99). DB_CONST stays empty, also matching
configure.ac: it is only set for a pre-ANSI compiler.

Applied after 0001: the two patches touch adjacent lines of the same table, and
this hunk's context lines are the two 0001 leaves alone.

diff -u -r a/dist/meson/db_subs.json b/dist/meson/db_subs.json
--- a/dist/meson/db_subs.json
+++ b/dist/meson/db_subs.json
@@ -10,4 +10,4 @@
   "DB_CONST": "",
-  "DB_PROTO1": "",
-  "DB_PROTO2": "",
+  "DB_PROTO1": "#undef __P",
+  "DB_PROTO2": "#define\t__P(protos)\tprotos",
   "db_seq_decl": "typedef int64_t db_seq_t;",
